(window.LEARN_C = window.LEARN_C || {})["mth-12-05"] = {"5.1":{"s":"A vector has both magnitude and direction; a scalar has magnitude only. Vectors are drawn as directed line segments and written in components along the unit vectors i, j, k. Types include the zero vector, unit vectors, equal, negative, collinear and coplanar vectors, and position vectors, which locate a point from the origin. The vector from A to B is b − a.","w":["AB = b − a (terminal minus initial), not a − b."]},"5.2":{"s":"The section formula gives the position vector of the point that divides the join of A(a) and B(b) in a given ratio, internally or externally. Special cases are the midpoint, (a + b)/2, and the centroid of a triangle, (a + b + c)/3, which divides each median in the ratio 2 : 1. The centroid of a tetrahedron is the average of its four vertices.","f":[{"x":"r = (k*b + a)/(k + 1)","n":"Point dividing AB internally in the ratio k : 1; externally r = (k b - a)/(k - 1).","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.153"},{"x":"r = (m*b - n*a)/(m - n)","n":"External division in the ratio m : n.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.153"},{"x":"g = (a + b + c)/3","n":"Centroid of triangle ABC; for a tetrahedron (a + b + c + d)/4.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.153"}],"w":["In the ratio m : n from A, m multiplies b (the far end), not a."]},"5.3":{"s":"The dot (scalar) product of two vectors is |a||b| cos θ, a number. It is zero for perpendicular vectors, gives the angle between two vectors, and in components is a₁b₁ + a₂b₂ + a₃b₃. It also gives projections: the scalar projection of b on a is a·b/|a|. The dot product is commutative and distributes over addition.","f":[{"x":"a.b = |a|*|b|*cos(theta)","n":"Scalar product; 0 <= theta <= pi.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.161"},{"x":"a.b = a_1*b_1 + a_2*b_2 + a_3*b_3","n":"In components.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.162"},{"x":"a.b/|a|","n":"Scalar projection of b on a; the vector projection is (a.b/|a|^2) a.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.162"}],"w":["a·b > 0 means the angle is acute, < 0 obtuse, = 0 right angle (for non-zero vectors)."]},"5.4":{"s":"The cross (vector) product a × b is a vector perpendicular to both a and b, of magnitude |a||b| sin θ, with direction by the right hand rule. It is found as a 3 × 3 determinant with i, j, k in the top row. Its magnitude is the area of the parallelogram on a and b. It is not commutative: b × a = −(a × b), and a × a = 0.","f":[{"x":"|a x b| = |a|*|b|*sin(theta)","n":"Magnitude of the vector product.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.171"},{"x":"A = |a x b|","n":"Area of the parallelogram with sides a and b; the triangle on them has half this area.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.171"}],"w":["i × j = k, j × k = i, k × i = j; reversing the order flips the sign."]},"5.5":{"s":"The scalar triple product [a b c] = a · (b × c) equals the 3 × 3 determinant of the components. It is the volume of the parallelepiped with coterminus edges a, b, c, and one sixth of it is the volume of the tetrahedron. It is zero when the three vectors are coplanar (or any two are collinear). Swapping two vectors changes its sign; swapping dot and cross does not change it.","f":[{"x":"V = a.(b x c) = [a b c]","n":"Volume of the parallelepiped with coterminus edges a, b, c (take the absolute value).","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.180"},{"x":"V = (1/6)*[a b c]","n":"Volume of the tetrahedron with coterminus edges a, b, c.","r":"Balbharati Maths XII Part 1, p.180"}],"w":["Three vectors are coplanar exactly when [a b c] = 0."]}};
